      "reviewedAt": "2026-08-24T14:08:33Z",
      "note": "Reviewed the selected exploit receipt and call trace, exact native and ERC-20 outflows, pinned reproduction, verified CEtherDelegate source, proxy creation trace, implementation slot, complete NewImplementation event history, historical runtime hashes, and the reported campaign loss. The pool-127 fETH delegator 0x26267e41ceca7c8e0f143554af707336f27fa051 executes the defect-bearing CEtherDelegate 0xd77e28a1b9a9cfe1fc2eee70e391c05d25853cbf. During borrow, that implementation sends ETH with an external call before recording the new account borrow; the callback exits the attacker's collateral market while the Comptroller still sees the old debt. The exploit transaction then extracts ETH, USDC, USDT, and FRAX from pool 127. Slot 0 selects 0xd77e28a1b9a9cfe1fc2eee70e391c05d25853cbf at proxy deployment block 13673508 and immediately before exploit block 14684814. The sole NewImplementation event through the exploit is the zero-to-d77e28 assignment in the creation transaction. The artifact runtime hash is 0x66fb56b08658840bdb33cc7c890cfbeaf4aac3d9aa248650cbb102854cbd9c9d at both historical checks. The selected transaction's exact outflows support the approximately $80 million reported multi-pool campaign total."
